  "title": "The Definition Comes Later",
  "subtitle": "Associate Professor Kwame Lindqvist and the Master of Priority Studies",
  "summary": "Associate Professor Kwame Lindqvist, Director of the Master of Priority Studies, sets out in his own words the gap his research occupies: the stretch between a priority receiving its budget and receiving its definition. Three of his most-cited papers, on a tailoring shop's turnaround guarantee, a retail chain's review software and a campus parking scorecard, serve as its cases in point. The profile closes on the body of work that has made him the most cited researcher in the School of Emergent Priorities.",
